{title: 003 - God Himself Is With Us}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #003 • WUNDERBARER KÖNIG}
{lyricist: Gerhard Tersteegen}
{composer: Joachim Neander}
{key: G}
{time: 2/2}
{tempo: 96}
{meta: hymn_number 3}
{meta: category Worship - Adoration and Praise}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]God Himself is [D]with us; [Em]Let us all a[B]dore Him,
[Em]And [G]with [C]awe [Am]ap[Bm]pear [G]be[D]fore [G]Him.
[G]God is here with[D]in us; [Em]Soul, in silence [B]fear Him,
[Em]Hum[G]bly, [C]fer[Am]vent[Bm]ly [G]draw [D]near [G]Him.
[G]Now His [C]own [D]who have [G]known [Am]God, [D7]in [G]wor[D]ship [Em]low[Bm]ly,
[C]Yield [Am]their [G]spir[D]its [D7]whol[G]ly.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Come, abide with[D]in me; [Em]Let my soul, like [B]Mary,
[Em]Be [G]Thine [C]earth[Am]ly [Bm]sanc[G]tu[D]ar[G]y.
[G]Come, indwelling [D]Spirit, [Em]With transfigured [B]splendor;
[Em]Love [G]and [C]hon[Am]or [Bm]will [G]I [D]ren[G]der.
[G]Where I [C]go [D]here be[G]low, [Am]Let [D7]me [G]bow [D]be[Em]fore [Bm]Thee,
[C]Know [Am]Thee [G]and [D]a[D7]dore [G]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Gladly we sur[D]render [Em]Earth's deceitful [B]treasures,
[Em]Pride [G]of [C]life [Am]and [Bm]sin[G]ful [D]plea[G]sures:
[G]Gladly, Lord, we [D]offer [Em]Thine to be for[B]ever,
[Em]Soul [G]and [C]life [Am]and [Bm]each [G]en[D]deav[G]or.
[G]Thou a[C]lone [D]shall be [G]known [Am]Lord [D7]of [G]all [D]our [Em]be[Bm]ing,
[C]Life's [Am]true [G]way [D]de[D7]cree[G]ing.
{end_of_verse}
